# Neo Drums parameters (docs/specs/machines.md §5, Neo Drums). The order is permanent: songs and presets store values by
# position. Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoDrums
namespace NeoBuzz.Drums
class NeoDrumsMachine
tracks 16
summary Synthesised drum kit in the TR-909 and TR-808 manner: kick, snare, clap, rim, closed and open hats (the closed one chokes the open one), low, mid and high toms, cowbell, crash and ride, each with its tune, decay, tone or snap (and the kick its sweep, click and drive), level and pan. Plays the General MIDI drum keys from C2 (kick C2, snare D2, closed hat F#2, open hat A#2), as Neo Sampler's Kit mode does, or per-track hit columns (BD, SD, … with a velocity) and an Accent column, as Buzz drum machines do. Velocity sets the level and opens the tone. Use it for drum parts.

# Each hit latches its voice's tune, decay and tone; level and pan follow while it sounds.
track Accent "Accent" switch | Accents every hit of this tick (notes and hit columns, on any track): louder by Accent gain, and brighter as Vel → tone says, as a TR-909's accent step does
track HitBD  "BD"  1 127 | Hits the kick at this velocity (1–127)
track HitSD  "SD"  1 127 | Hits the snare at this velocity (1–127)
track HitCP  "CP"  1 127 | Hits the clap at this velocity (1–127)
track HitRS  "RS"  1 127 | Hits the rim shot at this velocity (1–127)
track HitCH  "CH"  1 127 | Hits the closed hat (it chokes the open hat) at this velocity (1–127)
track HitOH  "OH"  1 127 | Hits the open hat at this velocity (1–127)
track HitLT  "LT"  1 127 | Hits the low tom at this velocity (1–127)
track HitMT  "MT"  1 127 | Hits the mid tom at this velocity (1–127)
track HitHT  "HT"  1 127 | Hits the high tom at this velocity (1–127)
track HitCB  "CB"  1 127 | Hits the cowbell at this velocity (1–127)
track HitCC  "CC"  1 127 | Hits the crash at this velocity (1–127)
track HitRC  "RC"  1 127 | Hits the ride at this velocity (1–127)

group Kit
Volume      "Volume"              0 720 600   db -60 12 inf               | Output level
    how Sets the overall output level of the kit, from -60 to +12 dB, or off.
    sound Use it to place the whole kit in the mix without changing the balance between drums.
Accent      "Accent gain"         0 120 60    db 0 12                     | How much louder an accented hit plays (a hit on a row with Accent): a TR-909's accent
    how Sets how much louder an accented hit plays, from 0 to 12 dB.
    sound Accented steps jump out of the pattern and give it a human, driving push.
VelLevel    "Vel → level"         0 1000 700   pct                         | How much velocity sets a hit's level: the gain is velocity^(2 × this) (100 %: velocity 64 is −12 dB; 0 %: every hit at full level)
    how Sets how strongly velocity changes the level of a hit, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound High values give a lively, dynamic kit, and 0 % makes every hit equally loud like a drum machine.
VelTone     "Vel → tone"          0 1000 500   pct                         | How much velocity (and accent) opens a hit: the kick's click and sweep, the snare's snap and tone, the toms' attack, the hats' and cymbals' tone; a hit at velocity 100 sounds as its parameters say
    how Sets how much velocity and accent open up the tone of a hit, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Harder hits get a sharper click, snap and brightness, and softer ones sound duller and rounder.

group Kick
KickTune    "Kick tune"           0 1000 365   freq 30 150                 | The body's pitch once its sweep has settled
    how Sets the pitch the kick body settles on, from 30 to 150 Hz.
    sound Low values give a deep sub thump, and higher ones a tighter, more tonal kick.
KickSweep   "Kick sweep"          0 480 300   lin 0 48 st 1               | How far above its tune the body starts, falling to it
    how Sets how far above its tune the kick starts, from 0 to 48 semitones.
    sound More sweep gives a stronger pitch-drop zap at the start, and none gives a flat sine boom.
KickSweepT  "Kick sweep time"     0 1000 548   time 0.002 0.2              | The sweep's time constant: the pitch is 63 % of the way down after this
    how Sets how quickly the kick falls from its start pitch to its tune, from 2 to 200 ms.
    sound Short sweeps sound clicky and tight, and long ones sound like a falling laser.
KickDecay   "Kick decay"          0 1000 525   time 0.05 4                 | Time for the body to fall 60 dB
    how Sets how long the kick body takes to die away, from 0.05 to 4 seconds.
    sound Short decays make a tight kick, and long ones a booming, held bass note.
KickClick   "Kick click"          0 1000 500   pct                         | Level of the attack's click (a short burst of high-passed noise)
    how Sets the level of the noisy click at the start of the kick, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound More click makes the beater attack audible and helps the kick cut through a mix.
KickPunch   "Kick punch"          0 1000 500   pct                         | How much louder the body starts (up to +12 dB at 100 %), falling back with the sweep: a TR-909's attack
    how Boosts the level of the kick's first moments by up to 12 dB, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound More punch gives a harder, more percussive attack that then settles into the body.
KickDrive   "Kick drive"          0 240 30    db 0 24                     | Saturation of the body, its level kept
    how Adds saturation to the kick body, from 0 to 24 dB, keeping its level.
    sound A little adds harmonics so the kick reads on small speakers, and a lot makes it gritty.
KickLevel   "Kick level"          0 660 600   db -60 6 inf                | Level of the kick
    how Sets the level of the kick, from -60 to +6 dB, or off.
    sound Use it to balance the kick against the other drums.
KickPan     "Kick pan"            0 200 100   lin -100 100 % 0            | Where the kick sits, from −100 % (left) to +100 % (right)
    how Places the kick from 100 % left to 100 % right.
    sound The centre is the usual place for a kick; moving it makes the kit feel off-balance.

group Snare
SnareTune   "Snare tune"          0 1000 424   freq 100 400                | The body's lower tone, once its short fall has settled (the upper sits an octave above)
    how Sets the lower tone of the snare body, from 100 to 400 Hz.
    sound Lower values sound fat and deep, and higher ones sound thin and tight.
SnareTone   "Snare tone"          0 1000 702   freq 1000 16000             | Centre of the snappy noise's band (from about half of it to 1.3 times it): brighter up
    how Sets the centre of the snappy noise band, from 1 to 16 kHz.
    sound Higher values give a bright, crisp rattle, and lower ones a darker, rounder one.
SnareSnap   "Snare snap"          0 1000 500   pct                         | The snappy noise against the body (0 %: the body alone)
    how Sets the level of the snappy noise against the body, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Zero leaves only the drum body, while more snap adds the sizzle of the snare wires.
SnareDecay  "Snare decay"         0 1000 486   time 0.05 2                 | Time for the snappy noise to fall 60 dB (the body takes about half)
    how Sets how long the snare noise rings, from 0.05 to 2 seconds.
    sound Short decays are dry and snappy, and long ones add a washy tail.
SnareLevel  "Snare level"         0 660 600   db -60 6 inf                | Level of the snare
    how Sets the level of the snare, from -60 to +6 dB, or off.
    sound Use it to balance the snare against the other drums.
SnarePan    "Snare pan"           0 200 100   lin -100 100 % 0            | Where the snare sits, from −100 % (left) to +100 % (right)
    how Places the snare from 100 % left to 100 % right.
    sound Centre is standard; a slight offset gives a more natural kit image.

group Clap
ClapTune    "Clap tune"           0 1000 301   freq 500 5000               | Centre of the clap's band-pass
    how Sets the centre frequency of the clap, from 500 Hz to 5 kHz.
    sound Lower values sound thick and woody, and higher ones sharp and papery.
ClapSpread  "Clap spread"         0 1000 630   time 0.002 0.03             | Time between the clap's three bursts
    how Sets the time between the clap's three bursts, from 2 to 30 ms.
    sound Short spreads sound like one tight clap, and longer ones like several people clapping.
ClapDecay   "Clap decay"          0 1000 674   time 0.05 2                 | Time for its tail to fall 60 dB
    how Sets how long the clap tail rings, from 0.05 to 2 seconds.
    sound Short decays are dry, and long ones add a roomy tail.
ClapLevel   "Clap level"          0 660 600   db -60 6 inf                | Level of the clap
    how Sets the level of the clap, from -60 to +6 dB, or off.
    sound Use it to balance the clap against the other drums.
ClapPan     "Clap pan"            0 200 100   lin -100 100 % 0            | Where the clap sits, from −100 % (left) to +100 % (right)
    how Places the clap from 100 % left to 100 % right.
    sound Off-centre claps help them sit beside the snare.

group Rim
RimTune     "Rim tune"            0 1000 398   freq 400 4000               | Pitch of the rim shot's highest ping (the others sit at half and 0.23 of it)
    how Sets the pitch of the rim shot, from 400 Hz to 4 kHz.
    sound Low values sound woody and dull, and high ones sound sharp and metallic.
RimDecay    "Rim decay"           0 1000 635   time 0.01 0.5               | Time for its pings to fall 60 dB
    how Sets how long the rim shot rings, from 10 to 500 ms.
    sound Short decays are a dry click, and longer ones let the ping ring.
RimLevel    "Rim level"           0 660 600   db -60 6 inf                | Level of the rim shot
    how Sets the level of the rim shot, from -60 to +6 dB, or off.
    sound Use it to balance the rim shot against the other drums.
RimPan      "Rim pan"             0 200 100   lin -100 100 % 0            | Where the rim shot sits, from −100 % (left) to +100 % (right)
    how Places the rim shot from 100 % left to 100 % right.
    sound Moving it aside gives a sparse beat more width.

group Closed hat
ChTune      "Closed hat tune"     0 240 120   lin -12 12 st 1             | Pitch of the six metallic oscillators, in semitones from the TR-808's
    how Shifts the pitch of the closed hat by up to 12 semitones either way.
    sound Lower values sound heavier and darker, and higher ones thinner and brighter.
ChTone      "Closed hat tone"     0 1000 636   freq 2000 16000             | Centre of the band the hats ring in (more above it, a little across the mids): brighter up
    how Sets the centre of the band the closed hat rings in, from 2 to 16 kHz.
    sound Higher values give a bright, sizzling hat, and lower ones a duller, softer one.
ChDecay     "Closed hat decay"    0 1000 452   time 0.01 1                 | Time to fall 60 dB
    how Sets how long the closed hat rings, from 10 ms to 1 second.
    sound Short decays tick tightly, and longer ones sound looser and more open.
ChLevel     "Closed hat level"    0 660 600   db -60 6 inf                | Level of the closed hat
    how Sets the level of the closed hat, from -60 to +6 dB, or off.
    sound Use it to balance the hat against the other drums.
ChPan       "Closed hat pan"      0 200 100   lin -100 100 % 0            | Where the closed hat sits, from −100 % (left) to +100 % (right)
    how Places the closed hat from 100 % left to 100 % right.
    sound Moving the hats slightly off-centre widens the top of the kit.

group Open hat
OhTune      "Open hat tune"       0 240 120   lin -12 12 st 1             | Pitch of the six metallic oscillators, in semitones from the TR-808's
    how Shifts the pitch of the open hat by up to 12 semitones either way.
    sound Lower values sound heavier and darker, and higher ones thinner and brighter.
OhTone      "Open hat tone"       0 1000 636   freq 2000 16000             | Centre of the band the hats ring in (more above it, a little across the mids): brighter up
    how Sets the centre of the band the open hat rings in, from 2 to 16 kHz.
    sound Higher values give a bright, sizzling hat, and lower ones a duller, softer one.
OhDecay     "Open hat decay"      0 1000 567   time 0.05 4                 | Time to fall 60 dB (a closed hat cuts it in 5 ms)
    how Sets how long the open hat rings, from 50 ms to 4 seconds; a closed hat cuts it off.
    sound Short decays sound like a half-open hat, and long ones like a wide, splashing hat.
OhLevel     "Open hat level"      0 660 600   db -60 6 inf                | Level of the open hat
    how Sets the level of the open hat, from -60 to +6 dB, or off.
    sound Use it to balance the hat against the other drums.
OhPan       "Open hat pan"        0 200 100   lin -100 100 % 0            | Where the open hat sits, from −100 % (left) to +100 % (right)
    how Places the open hat from 100 % left to 100 % right.
    sound Moving the hats slightly off-centre widens the top of the kit.

group Low tom
LtTune      "Low tom tune"        0 1000 147   freq 40 500                 | The tom's pitch once its sweep has settled (it starts 1.2 octaves above, falls an octave in about 25 ms, then the rest over about a second)
    how Sets the pitch the low tom settles on, from 40 to 500 Hz.
    sound Lower values sound big and booming, and higher ones short and tuned.
LtDecay     "Low tom decay"       0 1000 706   time 0.05 3                 | Time to fall 60 dB
    how Sets how long the low tom rings, from 0.05 to 3 seconds.
    sound Short decays are tight and dry, and long ones sing out like a floor tom.
LtTone      "Low tom tone"        0 1000 300   pct                         | Level of the attack's noise
    how Sets the level of the noisy attack of the low tom, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound More tone adds a stick-on-skin click, and less leaves a smooth, round sound.
LtLevel     "Low tom level"       0 660 600   db -60 6 inf                | Level of the low tom
    how Sets the level of the low tom, from -60 to +6 dB, or off.
    sound Use it to balance the tom against the other drums.
LtPan       "Low tom pan"         0 200 100   lin -100 100 % 0            | Where the low tom sits, from −100 % (left) to +100 % (right)
    how Places the low tom from 100 % left to 100 % right.
    sound Spreading the three toms from left to right gives fills a natural sweep.

group Mid tom
MtTune      "Mid tom tune"        0 1000 238   freq 40 500                 | The tom's pitch once its sweep has settled (it starts 1.2 octaves above, falls an octave in about 25 ms, then the rest over about a second)
    how Sets the pitch the mid tom settles on, from 40 to 500 Hz.
    sound Lower values sound big and booming, and higher ones short and tuned.
MtDecay     "Mid tom decay"       0 1000 626   time 0.05 3                 | Time to fall 60 dB
    how Sets how long the mid tom rings, from 0.05 to 3 seconds.
    sound Short decays are tight and dry, and long ones sing out like a floor tom.
MtTone      "Mid tom tone"        0 1000 300   pct                         | Level of the attack's noise
    how Sets the level of the noisy attack of the mid tom, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound More tone adds a stick-on-skin click, and less leaves a smooth, round sound.
MtLevel     "Mid tom level"       0 660 600   db -60 6 inf                | Level of the mid tom
    how Sets the level of the mid tom, from -60 to +6 dB, or off.
    sound Use it to balance the tom against the other drums.
MtPan       "Mid tom pan"         0 200 100   lin -100 100 % 0            | Where the mid tom sits, from −100 % (left) to +100 % (right)
    how Places the mid tom from 100 % left to 100 % right.
    sound Spreading the three toms from left to right gives fills a natural sweep.

group High tom
HtTune      "High tom tune"       0 1000 294   freq 40 500                 | The tom's pitch once its sweep has settled (it starts 1.2 octaves above, falls an octave in about 25 ms, then the rest over about a second)
    how Sets the pitch the high tom settles on, from 40 to 500 Hz.
    sound Lower values sound big and booming, and higher ones short and tuned.
HtDecay     "High tom decay"      0 1000 626   time 0.05 3                 | Time to fall 60 dB
    how Sets how long the high tom rings, from 0.05 to 3 seconds.
    sound Short decays are tight and dry, and long ones sing out like a floor tom.
HtTone      "High tom tone"       0 1000 300   pct                         | Level of the attack's noise
    how Sets the level of the noisy attack of the high tom, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound More tone adds a stick-on-skin click, and less leaves a smooth, round sound.
HtLevel     "High tom level"      0 660 600   db -60 6 inf                | Level of the high tom
    how Sets the level of the high tom, from -60 to +6 dB, or off.
    sound Use it to balance the tom against the other drums.
HtPan       "High tom pan"        0 200 100   lin -100 100 % 0            | Where the high tom sits, from −100 % (left) to +100 % (right)
    how Places the high tom from 100 % left to 100 % right.
    sound Spreading the three toms from left to right gives fills a natural sweep.

group Cowbell
CbTune      "Cowbell tune"        0 1000 371   freq 300 1500               | Pitch of the lower of its two square waves (the upper sits 1.48 times above)
    how Sets the pitch of the cowbell, from 300 Hz to 1.5 kHz.
    sound Lower values clunk like a big bell, and higher ones ring like a small one.
CbDecay     "Cowbell decay"       0 1000 651   time 0.02 2                 | Time for its tail to fall 60 dB (the attack falls faster)
    how Sets how long the cowbell rings, from 20 ms to 2 seconds.
    sound Short decays are a dry clack, and longer ones a ringing bell.
CbLevel     "Cowbell level"       0 660 600   db -60 6 inf                | Level of the cowbell
    how Sets the level of the cowbell, from -60 to +6 dB, or off.
    sound Use it to balance the cowbell against the other drums.
CbPan       "Cowbell pan"         0 200 100   lin -100 100 % 0            | Where the cowbell sits, from −100 % (left) to +100 % (right)
    how Places the cowbell from 100 % left to 100 % right.
    sound Moving it aside keeps it from crowding the centre.

group Crash
CcTune      "Crash tune"          0 240 120   lin -12 12 st 1             | Pitch of the six metallic oscillators, in semitones from where they sit
    how Shifts the pitch of the crash by up to 12 semitones either way.
    sound Lower values sound bigger and darker, and higher ones lighter and thinner.
CcTone      "Crash tone"          0 1000 452   freq 1000 16000             | Centre of the wide band it rings in (more above it, a little across the mids): brighter up
    how Sets the centre of the band the crash rings in, from 1 to 16 kHz.
    sound Higher values give a brighter, harsher cymbal, and lower ones a softer, darker one.
CcDecay     "Crash decay"         0 1000 546   time 0.2 8                  | Time to fall 60 dB
    how Sets how long the crash rings, from 0.2 to 8 seconds.
    sound Short decays are a quick accent, and long ones a washy cymbal that fills the space.
CcLevel     "Crash level"         0 660 600   db -60 6 inf                | Level of the crash
    how Sets the level of the crash, from -60 to +6 dB, or off.
    sound Use it to balance the cymbal against the other drums.
CcPan       "Crash pan"           0 200 100   lin -100 100 % 0            | Where the crash sits, from −100 % (left) to +100 % (right)
    how Places the crash from 100 % left to 100 % right.
    sound A slight offset gives the cymbal a place in the kit's stereo picture.

group Ride
RcTune      "Ride tune"           0 240 120   lin -12 12 st 1             | Pitch of the six metallic oscillators, in semitones from where they sit
    how Shifts the pitch of the ride by up to 12 semitones either way.
    sound Lower values sound bigger and darker, and higher ones lighter and thinner.
RcTone      "Ride tone"           0 1000 615   freq 1000 16000             | Centre of the band it pings in (more above it, a little across the mids): brighter up
    how Sets the centre of the band the ride rings in, from 1 to 16 kHz.
    sound Higher values give a brighter, harsher cymbal, and lower ones a softer, darker one.
RcDecay     "Ride decay"          0 1000 596   time 0.2 8                  | Time to fall 60 dB
    how Sets how long the ride rings, from 0.2 to 8 seconds.
    sound Short decays are a quick accent, and long ones a washy cymbal that fills the space.
RcLevel     "Ride level"          0 660 600   db -60 6 inf                | Level of the ride
    how Sets the level of the ride, from -60 to +6 dB, or off.
    sound Use it to balance the cymbal against the other drums.
RcPan       "Ride pan"            0 200 100   lin -100 100 % 0            | Where the ride sits, from −100 % (left) to +100 % (right)
    how Places the ride from 100 % left to 100 % right.
    sound A slight offset gives the cymbal a place in the kit's stereo picture.
